  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A pest controller was responsible for humanely reducing the number of mice within a hotel. If there were $720$ mice initially and $\\frac{5}{6}$ of mice were removed from the hotel every day, how many mice remained in the hotel after two days?",
  "worked_solution": "Since the number of mice reduced by $\\frac{5}{6}$ per day, then only $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the mice from the previous day remained.\n\nSo we have:\n\n- At the start, there were $720$ mice.\n\n- After $1$ day, there were $720\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})$ mice.\n\n- After $2$ days, there were $720\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}$ mice.\n\nEvaluating the last expression, we get\n\n$$\n720\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}=20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $2$ days only $20$ mice remained.",
